From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:39:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] impeller: destroy the image view of the embedder's onscreen
 image

GPUSurfaceVulkanImpeller::AcquireFrame wraps the VkImage the embedder
hands it each frame (the path without a swapchain of its own,
FlutterVulkanImage) in a WrappedTextureSourceVK with an image view it
creates for it. The view was a plain vk::ImageView that nothing
destroyed: the wrapper's destructor is empty and the image, which the
embedder owns, is not destroyed either. So each frame left one
VkImageView behind.

The wrapper now owns the view as a vk::UniqueImageView
(createImageViewUnique), so it is destroyed with the wrapper, once the
frame's command buffers no longer hold the texture source. Upstream's
current code does the same: the wrapper, now in
impeller/renderer/backend/vulkan/texture_wrapper_vk.cc
(WrapTextureSourceVK), keeps the view in a vk::UniqueImageView. Which
upstream change made the view owned was not traced.

Measured on a Raspberry Pi 5 with the AGL Flutter instrument cluster in
a Xen DomU, drawing through Venus (virtio-gpu Vulkan), 2026-10-19/20. A
census of the host renderer's live Vulkan objects (a diagnostic build of
virglrenderer, not in this tree):

    before: VK_OBJECT_TYPE_IMAGE_VIEW 3361 -> 28560 in 7 minutes, 60 a second
            (one a frame), every other type flat; the host renderer's
            anonymous memory grew about 1.76 MB a minute (about 500 bytes a
            view) and ran DomD out of memory after about 14 hours once
    after:  VK_OBJECT_TYPE_IMAGE_VIEW 35 and 863-868 objects in all, flat
            for 75 minutes; the host renderer's anonymous memory stayed at
            14916 kB over that time, against 1.76 MB a minute before

The guest's flutter process grew much less (a view is a small handle
there): 97.9 -> 99.1 MB in 5 minutes before, peaking at 99.7 (0.2-0.3 MB
a minute), and 15-18 MB for the 75 minutes after, which is why the leak
first looked like the host's.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [engine 3.32.5 only: upstream's current code
 already owns this view (texture_wrapper_vk.cc in impeller's Vulkan backend)]
---
--- a/engine/src/flutter/shell/gpu/gpu_surface_vulkan_impeller.cc
+++ b/engine/src/flutter/shell/gpu/gpu_surface_vulkan_impeller.cc
@@ -25,25 +25,29 @@
 class WrappedTextureSourceVK : public impeller::TextureSourceVK {
  public:
   explicit WrappedTextureSourceVK(impeller::vk::Image image,
-                                  impeller::vk::ImageView image_view,
+                                  impeller::vk::UniqueImageView image_view,
                                   impeller::TextureDescriptor desc)
-      : TextureSourceVK(desc), image_(image), image_view_(image_view) {}
+      : TextureSourceVK(desc),
+        image_(image),
+        image_view_(std::move(image_view)) {}
 
   ~WrappedTextureSourceVK() {}
 
  private:
   impeller::vk::Image GetImage() const override { return image_; }
 
-  impeller::vk::ImageView GetImageView() const override { return image_view_; }
+  impeller::vk::ImageView GetImageView() const override {
+    return image_view_.get();
+  }
 
   impeller::vk::ImageView GetRenderTargetView() const override {
-    return image_view_;
+    return image_view_.get();
   }
 
   bool IsSwapchainImage() const override { return true; }
 
   impeller::vk::Image image_;
-  impeller::vk::ImageView image_view_;
+  impeller::vk::UniqueImageView image_view_;
 };
 
 GPUSurfaceVulkanImpeller::GPUSurfaceVulkanImpeller(
@@ -177,7 +181,7 @@
     view_info.image = vk_image;
 
     auto [result, image_view] =
-        context_vk.GetDevice().createImageView(view_info);
+        context_vk.GetDevice().createImageViewUnique(view_info);
     if (result != impeller::vk::Result::eSuccess) {
       FML_LOG(ERROR) << "Failed to create image view for provided image: "
                      << impeller::vk::to_string(result);
@@ -191,7 +195,8 @@
     }
 
     auto wrapped_onscreen =
-        std::make_shared<WrappedTextureSourceVK>(vk_image, image_view, desc);
+        std::make_shared<WrappedTextureSourceVK>(vk_image, std::move(image_view),
+                                                 desc);
     auto surface = impeller::SurfaceVK::WrapSwapchainImage(
         transients_, wrapped_onscreen, [&]() -> bool { return true; });
     impeller::RenderTarget render_target = surface->GetRenderTarget();
